# CAPTURED AGAINST autoloop_local.sh v2 (after H116). Same arms, same file.

F5 CONTROL — the gate must be able to REFUSE, or F4 proves nothing:
  rc=1   no-falsifier-section       | REFUSE: program states no falsifier. Rule 2 cannot be applied to a program

F4 — what does it actually require?
  rc=1   heading-only-EMPTY         | REFUSE: program has a '## Falsifier' HEADING and no falsifier under it.
  rc=1   heading-plus-blank-line    | REFUSE: program has a '## Falsifier' HEADING and no falsifier under it.
  rc=0   heading-with-real-text     | falsifier : present with a body; program.md last committed at UNCOMMITTED
  rc=0   heading-saying-none        | falsifier : present with a body; program.md last committed at UNCOMMITTED

  The gate is a grep for the heading. Its header claims the falsifier
  was 'stated BEFORE the run' -- a TEMPORAL property. A run-time grep can
  only decide an EXISTENTIAL one, and above it decides even less than that:
  it decides whether a HEADING is present.

§10 check — the arms wrote nothing outside this spike:
  .autoloop/state entries: 0 (expect 0)
  proposed/autoloop-*:     0 (expect 0)
